"Cancellation for 4-manifolds with virtually abelian fundamental group (https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.05968)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.3 years ago; Title: Cancellation for 4-manifolds with virtually abelian fundamental group ... In particular, if $\\pi$ is finite then $n=0$, hence $X$ and $Y$ are $2$-stably homeomorphic, which is one $S^2 \\times S^2$ summand in excess of the cancellation theorem of Hambleton--Kreck.\nTitle: Cancellation for 4-manifolds with virtually abelian fundamental group\nAuthors: Qayum Khan\nDate: Mon Jun 20 04:22:11 2016\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are compact connected topological 4-manifolds with fundamental group $\\pi$. For any $r \\geqslant 0$, $Y$ is $r$-stably homeomorphic to $X$ if $Y \\# r(S^2 \\times S^2)$ is homeomorphic to $X \\# r(S^2\\times S^2)$. How close is stable homeomorphism to homeomorphism? When the common fundamental group $\\pi$ is virtually abelian, we show that large $r$ can be diminished to $n+2$, where $\\pi$ has a finite-index subgroup that is free-abelian of rank $n$. In particular, if $\\pi$ is finite then $n=0$, hence $X$ and $Y$ are $2$-stably homeomorphic, which is one $S^2 \\times S^2$ summand in excess of the cancellation theorem of Hambleton--Kreck. The last section is a case-study investigation of the homeomorphism classification of closed manifolds in the tangential homotopy type of $X = X_- \\# X_+$, where $X_\\pm$ are closed nonorientable topological 4-manifolds whose fundamental groups have order two.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTopology and its Applications 220 (2017) 14–30 (https://qkhan.pages.iu.edu/research/ARTICLES/CancellationTop4Mfld.pdf)\nciteturn1search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Cancellation for 4-manifolds with virtually abelian fundamental ... Suppose X is a compact connected smooth 4-manifold, with fundamental group π and orientation char-\nTopology and its Applications 220 (2017) 14–30\nContents li